      "body": "# Description\n\nAn exception thrown by an `nvte_ep_*` call inside a JAX EP FFI handler (e.g., `handle_mem buffer is too small`) propagates through XLA, which is not exception-safe. On GB200 CI this segfaults the process (`test_primitive_prepare_rejects_undersized_handle`) instead of surfacing a Python error. The handlers now catch the exception and return an XLA FFI internal error, as `EpInstantiate` and the borrowed-comm bootstrap already do.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [ ] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\n- [ ] Code refactoring\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add an `ffi_guard` helper in `ffi.h` that runs a callable, returns `ffi_internal_error(...)` if it throws, and otherwise returns `ffi_with_cuda_error_check()`.\n- Use it around the `nvte_ep_*` calls in `EpPrepareFFI`, `EpDispatchFFI`, `EpPrepareAndDispatchFFI`, `EpCombineFFI`, `EpDispatchBwdFFI` and `EpCombineBwdFFI`.\n\n# Checklist:\n\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n- [x] The functionality is complete\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\n- [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works\n- [x] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\n",
